@comment{
  Paste one BibTeX entry per paper below. The home page and publication.html?id=<key> are built from this file.

  Standard fields (title, author, year, month, journal/booktitle, url, doi, eprint) are rendered and kept in "Copy BibTeX".
  Site-only fields (shown on the site, stripped from "Copy BibTeX"):
    github, project, pdf, video, slides : link buttons
    tldr                                : one-line subtitle on the paper page
    cover                               : hero image file inside posts/<key>/, e.g. cover.jpg
    abstract                            : shown when there is no blog post

  Blog post (optional): create a folder posts/<key>/ with an index.md in Markdown, and put its images and
  files in the same folder. Reference them by filename: ![Overview](figure1.png). Each "## Heading" becomes
  a numbered section, $x$ and $$x$$ render as math, and raw HTML (<figure>, <video>, <iframe>) works too.

  Example:
  @inproceedings[petroni2026example,
    title     = [A Short Paper Title],
    author    = [Sigillo, Luigi and Petroni, Fabio],
    booktitle = [Conference Name],
    year      = [2026],
    month     = [September],
    eprint    = [2609.01234],
    github    = [https://github.com/petronilab/example],
    tldr      = [One sentence on what the paper does.],
    cover     = [cover.jpg]
  ]
  (brackets stand in for curly braces so this example is not parsed)
}

